IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part 3 of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia), sections 14 to 26: general interpretative provisions.
-- Where a section hands a judgment to the reader (which interpretation best achieves a purpose, whether an act is reasonably required,
-- whether a meaning is manifestly absurd), the judgment is a plain true/false input.
-- Dates that bound a section ("after 1 January 1873", "after 20 June 1990") are compared with the day an Act was passed or an instrument made.

§ `Part 3 -- General interpretative provisions (sections 14 to 26)`

§§ `14 -- Interpretation best achieving purpose or object`

DECLARE `How the purpose or object is known` IS ONE OF
    `expressly stated in the Act or instrument`
    `not expressly stated`

-- src:311 | (1) In interpreting a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, the interpretation that best achieves the purpose or object of the Act or the instrument (whether or not that purpose or object is expressly stated in the Act or instrument) is to be preferred to any other interpretation.
@ref s 14(1) (src:311)
GIVEN `how the purpose or object is known` IS A `How the purpose or object is known`
      `this interpretation best achieves the purpose or object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an interpretation is to be preferred to any other` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the purpose or object is known`
        WHEN `expressly stated in the Act or instrument` THEN IF `this interpretation best achieves the purpose or object` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `not expressly stated` THEN IF `this interpretation best achieves the purpose or object` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:312 | (2) This section does not operate to create or extend any criminal liability.
@ref s 14(2) (src:312)
`section 14 operates to create or extend criminal liability` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `15 -- Interpretation so as not to exceed legislative power`

DECLARE `Part of the reach of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `a part within the power`
    `a part in excess of the power`

-- src:314 | (1) An Act or a legislative instrument is to be interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the legislative power of the State.
@ref s 15(1) (src:314)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of the reach of a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act or legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(1)` MEANS
    part EQUALS `a part within the power`

-- src:315 | (2) A legislative instrument made under an Act is to be interpreted as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the power to make the instrument conferred by the Act.
@ref s 15(2) (src:315)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of the reach of a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(2)` MEANS
    part EQUALS `a part within the power`

-- src:316 | (3) If a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument would, but for this section, be interpreted as being in excess of power, the provision is valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of power.
@ref s 15(3) (src:316)
GIVEN part IS A `Part of the reach of a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a provision has effect as to this part of its reach under section 15(3)` MEANS
    part EQUALS `a part within the power`

§§ `16 -- Use of extrinsic material in interpretation`

-- Consideration may be given to material not forming part of the Act that is capable of assisting:
-- (a) to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning; or (b) to determine the meaning if (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure,
-- or (ii) the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
-- src:318 | (1) In the interpretation of a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, if any material not forming part of the Act or instrument is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision, consideration may be given to that material—
-- src:319 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or instrument and the purpose or object underlying the Act or instrument and, in the case of a legislative instrument, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the instrument was made); or
-- src:320 | (b) to determine the meaning of the provision—
-- src:321 | (i) if the provision is ambiguous or obscure; or
-- src:322 | (ii) if the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or instrument and the purpose or object underlying the Act or instrument and, in the case of a legislative instrument, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the instrument was made) leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
@ref s 16(1) (src:318-322)
GIVEN `material not forming part of the Act or instrument is capable of assisting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary meaning produces a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`consideration may be given to the material` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `material not forming part of the Act or instrument is capable of assisting` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the purpose is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning`
            OR `the provision is ambiguous or obscure`
            OR `the ordinary meaning produces a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Material that may be considered under section 16(2)` IS ONE OF
    `matters set out in the document containing the text as printed or published`
    `a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or similar body laid before Parliament`
    `a relevant report of a committee of the Parliament`
    `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the Act`
    `an explanatory memorandum or other relevant document laid before Parliament by the Minister or member introducing the Bill`
    `the second reading speech`
    `a document declared by the Act to be a relevant document`
    `relevant material in the Minutes of Proceedings, the Votes and Proceedings or an official record of debates`
    `other material`

-- src:323 | (2) Without limiting the effect of subsection (1), the material that may be considered in accordance with that subsection in the interpretation of a provision includes the following:
-- src:324 | (a) all matters not forming part of the Act or instrument that are set out in the document containing the text of the Act or instrument as printed or published by the Government Printer or as published under the Legislation Revision and Publication Act 2002;
-- src:325 | (b) any relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body that was laid before either House of the Parliament before the provision was enacted or made;
-- src:326 | (c) any relevant report of a committee of the Parliament or of either House of the Parliament before the provision was enacted or made;
-- src:327 | (d) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the Act;
-- src:328 | (e) any explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill for the Act, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or furnished to the members of, either House of the Parliament by a Minister or other member of Parliament introducing the Bill before the provision was enacted or made;
-- src:329 | (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a Minister or other member of Parliament on the occasion of the moving by that Minister or member of a motion that the Bill for the Act be read a second time in that House;
-- src:330 | (g) any document (whether or not a document to which a preceding paragraph applies) that is declared by the Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section;
-- src:331 | (h) any relevant material in the Minutes of Proceedings or the Votes and Proceedings of either House of Parliament or in any official record of debates in Parliament or either House of Parliament.
@ref s 16(2) (src:323-331)
GIVEN material IS A `Material that may be considered under section 16(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the material is included among the material that may be considered` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
        WHEN `other material` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Matter to which regard must be had under section 16(3)` IS ONE OF
    `the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision`
    `the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage`
    `another relevant matter`

-- src:332 | (3) In determining whether consideration should be given to any material, or in considering the weight to be given to any material, regard must be had, in addition to any other relevant matters, to—
-- src:333 | (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision (taking into account its context in the Act or instrument and the purpose or object underlying the Act or instrument and, in the case of a legislative instrument, the purpose or object underlying the Act under which the instrument was made); and
-- src:334 | (b) the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage.
@ref s 16(3) (src:332-334)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter to which regard must be had under section 16(3)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`regard must be had to the matter in deciding whether to consider material` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `another relevant matter` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `17 to 20 -- Always speaking, re-enactment, material that is part of an Act, amending Acts, examples`

DECLARE `Tense of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `the present tense`
    `the future tense`
    `any other tense`

-- src:336 | An Act or a legislative instrument will be considered as speaking at all times, and every provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, whether expressed in the present or the future tense, will be applied to the circumstances as they arise, so that effect may be given to each provision according to its spirit, true intent and meaning.
@ref s 17 (src:336)
GIVEN tense IS A `Tense of a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a provision is applied to the circumstances as they arise` MEANS
    CONSIDER tense
        WHEN `the present tense` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the future tense` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `any other tense` THEN NOTHING

-- src:338 | The enactment or re‑enactment of a provision of an Act that has been construed in a particular manner (judicially or otherwise) in this State or elsewhere creates no presumption that Parliament has sanctioned or approved that construction.
@ref s 18 (src:338)
`re-enactment of a provision that has been construed creates a presumption that Parliament sanctioned the construction` MEANS JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument` IS ONE OF
    `anything described as an editorial note`
    `material appearing under the heading Legislative History`
    `an appendix setting out a table of divisional penalty and expiation fee amounts that specifies that it is for convenience of reference only`
    `an appendix setting out such a table that does not so specify`
    `anything else appearing in it`

-- src:340 | (1) Except as provided in subsection (2), everything appearing in an Act or a legislative instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:341 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to—
-- src:342 | (a) anything described as an editorial note; or
-- src:343 | (b) material appearing under the heading "Legislative History"; or
-- src:344 | (c) an appendix setting out a table of divisional penalty and expiation fee amounts that specifies that it is for convenience of reference only.
@ref s 19 (src:340-344)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
        WHEN `anything described as an editorial note` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `material appearing under the heading Legislative History` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an appendix setting out a table of divisional penalty and expiation fee amounts that specifies that it is for convenience of reference only` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `an appendix setting out such a table that does not so specify` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `anything else appearing in it` THEN TRUE

-- src:346 | An Act or legislative instrument that amends another Act or legislative instrument must be construed with the other Act or instrument as part of that other Act or instrument.
@ref s 19A (src:346)
GIVEN `the Act or legislative instrument amends another Act or legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an amending Act or instrument must be construed as part of the amended Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `the Act or legislative instrument amends another Act or legislative instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `What an example may do to the meaning of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `extend it`
    `limit it`

-- src:348 | An example included in an Act or a legislative instrument—
-- src:349 | (a) is not exhaustive; and
-- src:350 | (b) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the provision of the Act or legislative instrument to which it relates.
@ref s 20 (src:348-350)
`an example included in an Act or legislative instrument is exhaustive` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- src:350 | (b) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the provision of the Act or legislative instrument to which it relates.
@ref s 20(b) (src:350)
GIVEN effect IS A `What an example may do to the meaning of a provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an example may do this to the meaning of the provision it relates to` MEANS
    effect EQUALS `extend it`

§§ `21 -- Things to be done by Governor`

-- src:352 | If, in an Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, after 1 January 1873, the Governor is authorised or required to do any act, matter or thing, it will be taken to mean that the act, matter or thing may or must be done by the Governor with the advice and consent of the Executive Council.
@ref s 21 (src:352)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed or the legislative instrument was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Governor's act is taken to be done with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` MEANS
    JUST (`the day the Act was passed or the legislative instrument was made` GREATER THAN (Date 1 1 1873))

§§ `22 -- Determining whether Act or instrument binds Crown`

-- Section 22(2): an Act or instrument passed or made after 20 June 1990 that amends one passed or made before that date.
-- src:355 | (2) If an Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, after 20 June 1990 amends an Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, before that date, the question whether the amendment binds the Crown will be determined in accordance with subsection (3).
@ref s 22(2) (src:355)
GIVEN `the day the amending Act was passed or instrument made` IS A DATE
      `the day the amended Act was passed or instrument made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`whether the amendment binds the Crown is decided by section 22(3)` MEANS
        `the day the amending Act was passed or instrument made` GREATER THAN (Date 20 6 1990)
    AND `the day the amended Act was passed or instrument made` LESS THAN (Date 20 6 1990)

-- Section 22(3): passed or made on or before 20 June 1990: bound only if it expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown.
-- src:356 | (3) An Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, on or before 20 June 1990 will only be taken to bind the Crown if the Act or instrument expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown.
@ref s 22(3) (src:356)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed or instrument made` IS A DATE
      `it expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an Act passed or instrument made on or before 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act was passed or instrument made` AT MOST (Date 20 6 1990)
    THEN (IF `it expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 22(1): passed or made after 20 June 1990: taken to bind the Crown unless the contrary intention appears, subject to s 22(2).
-- src:354 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), an Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, after 20 June 1990 will, unless the contrary intention appears (either expressly or by implication), be taken to bind the Crown, but not so as to impose any criminal liability on the Crown.
@ref s 22(1) (src:354)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed or instrument made` IS A DATE
      `the Act or instrument amends one passed or made before 20 June 1990` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears, expressly or by implication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the Act was passed or instrument made` AT MOST (Date 20 6 1990) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the Act or instrument amends one passed or made before 20 June 1990` THEN JUST `it expressly, or by necessary implication, binds the Crown`
        IF `the contrary intention appears, expressly or by implication` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:354 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), an Act passed, or a legislative instrument made, after 20 June 1990 will, unless the contrary intention appears (either expressly or by implication), be taken to bind the Crown, but not so as to impose any criminal liability on the Crown.
@ref s 22(1) (src:354)
`binding the Crown under section 22(1) imposes criminal liability on the Crown` MEANS JUST FALSE

-- Section 22(4) and (5): the Crown's immunity from criminal liability extends to an agent of the Crown in respect of an act within the scope
-- of the agent's obligations, unless the contrary is expressed.
-- src:357 | (4) If an Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, (whether passed or made before or after 20 June 1990) binds the Crown but not so as to impose any criminal liability on the Crown, the Crown's immunity from criminal liability extends (unless the contrary intention is expressed) to an agent of the Crown in respect of an act within the scope of the agent's obligations.
@ref s 22(4) (src:357)
GIVEN `the Act or provision binds the Crown but not so as to impose any criminal liability on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within the scope of the agent's obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act binds the Crown` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Act or provision binds the Crown but not so as to impose any criminal liability on it` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the contrary is expressed` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the act is within the scope of the agent's obligations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:358 | (5) If an Act or a legislative instrument, or a provision of an Act or a legislative instrument, (whether passed or made before or after 20 June 1990) does not bind the Crown, the Crown's immunity extends (unless the contrary intention is expressed) to an agent of the Crown in respect of an act within the scope of the agent's obligations.
@ref s 22(5) (src:358)
GIVEN `the Act or provision does not bind the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within the scope of the agent's obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is expressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act does not bind the Crown` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Act or provision does not bind the Crown` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the contrary is expressed` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the act is within the scope of the agent's obligations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Section 22(6): for the purposes of section 22.
DECLARE `Capacity of the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `the Crown in right of this State`
    `the Crown in any other capacity`

-- src:359 | (6) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:360 | (a) a reference to the Crown extends not only to the Crown in right of this State but also (so far as the legislative power of the State permits) to the Crown in any other capacity; and
@ref s 22(6)(a) (src:359-360)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Capacity of the Crown`, `the legislative power of the State permits it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the Crown extends to the Crown in this capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
        WHEN `the Crown in right of this State` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Crown in any other capacity` THEN `the legislative power of the State permits it`

DECLARE `Kind of agent of the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `an instrumentality of the Crown`
    `an officer of the Crown`
    `an employee of the Crown`
    `a contractor or other person who carries out functions on behalf of the Crown`
    `someone else`

-- src:361 | (b) a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to an instrumentality, officer or employee of the Crown or a contractor or other person who carries out functions on behalf of the Crown; and
@ref s 22(6)(b) (src:361)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of agent of the Crown`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:362 | (c) an agent acts within the scope of the agent's obligations if the act is reasonably required for carrying out of obligations or functions imposed on, or assigned to, the agent.
@ref s 22(6)(c) (src:362)
GIVEN `the act is reasonably required for carrying out obligations or functions imposed on, or assigned to, the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an agent acts within the scope of the agent's obligations` MEANS
    `the act is reasonably required for carrying out obligations or functions imposed on, or assigned to, the agent`

§§ `23 to 26 -- Establishment of the State, the Australia Acts, public Acts, enacting words`

-- src:364 | The State is taken to have been established on 28 December 1836.
@ref s 23 (src:364)
`the day the State is taken to have been established` MEANS Date 28 12 1836

-- src:366 | Each provision of an Act or a legislative instrument enacted or made, or purporting to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts is as valid as it would have been, and has the same effect as it would have had, if the Australia Acts had been in operation at the time of its enactment or making or purported enactment or making.
@ref s 24 (src:366)
GIVEN `it was enacted or made, or purports to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a provision has the effect it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation` MEANS
    IF `it was enacted or made, or purports to have been enacted or made, before the commencement of the Australia Acts` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:368 | An Act passed after 1 January 1873 is taken to be a public Act.
@ref s 25 (src:368)
GIVEN `the day the Act was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an Act is taken to be a public Act` MEANS
    IF `the day the Act was passed` GREATER THAN (Date 1 1 1873) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:370 | There is no requirement for a provision or portion of an Act to have separate enacting words in order to have effect as a substantive enactment.
@ref s 26 (src:370)
`a provision or portion of an Act needs separate enacting words to have effect as a substantive enactment` MEANS JUST FALSE

§§ `Tests`

-- s 14
#ASSERT `an interpretation is to be preferred to any other` `expressly stated in the Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an interpretation is to be preferred to any other` `not expressly stated` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an interpretation is to be preferred to any other` `not expressly stated` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an interpretation is to be preferred to any other` `expressly stated in the Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `section 14 operates to create or extend criminal liability` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15
#ASSERT `an Act or legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(1)` `a part within the power`
#ASSERT NOT (`an Act or legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(1)` `a part in excess of the power`)
#ASSERT `a legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(2)` `a part within the power`
#ASSERT NOT (`a legislative instrument operates as to this part of its reach under section 15(2)` `a part in excess of the power`)
#ASSERT `a provision has effect as to this part of its reach under section 15(3)` `a part within the power`
#ASSERT NOT (`a provision has effect as to this part of its reach under section 15(3)` `a part in excess of the power`)
-- s 16(1)
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `consideration may be given to the material` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(2) and (3)
#ASSERT `the material is included among the material that may be considered` `the second reading speech` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is included among the material that may be considered` `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is included among the material that may be considered` `relevant material in the Minutes of Proceedings, the Votes and Proceedings or an official record of debates` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the material is included among the material that may be considered` `other material` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regard must be had to the matter in deciding whether to consider material` `the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `regard must be had to the matter in deciding whether to consider material` `the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `regard must be had to the matter in deciding whether to consider material` `another relevant matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 17 to 20
#ASSERT `a provision is applied to the circumstances as they arise` `the present tense` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision is applied to the circumstances as they arise` `the future tense` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision is applied to the circumstances as they arise` `any other tense` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `re-enactment of a provision that has been construed creates a presumption that Parliament sanctioned the construction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `anything described as an editorial note`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `material appearing under the heading Legislative History`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `an appendix setting out a table of divisional penalty and expiation fee amounts that specifies that it is for convenience of reference only`)
#ASSERT `a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `an appendix setting out such a table that does not so specify`
#ASSERT `a thing appearing in an Act or legislative instrument is part of it` `anything else appearing in it`
#ASSERT `an amending Act or instrument must be construed as part of the amended Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an amending Act or instrument must be construed as part of the amended Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an example included in an Act or legislative instrument is exhaustive` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an example may do this to the meaning of the provision it relates to` `extend it`
#ASSERT NOT (`an example may do this to the meaning of the provision it relates to` `limit it`)
-- s 21: 1 January 1873 itself is not "after".
#ASSERT `the Governor's act is taken to be done with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` (Date 2 1 1873) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Governor's act is taken to be done with the advice and consent of the Executive Council` (Date 1 1 1873) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22: 20 June 1990 itself is "on or before", not "after".
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 21 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 21 6 1990) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 20 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 21 6 1990) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made after 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 21 6 1990) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made on or before 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 20 6 1990) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made on or before 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 20 6 1990) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made on or before 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 19 6 1990) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `an Act passed or instrument made on or before 20 June 1990 is taken to bind the Crown` (Date 21 6 1990) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `binding the Crown under section 22(1) imposes criminal liability on the Crown` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `whether the amendment binds the Crown is decided by section 22(3)` (Date 1 7 1990) (Date 1 1 1980)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether the amendment binds the Crown is decided by section 22(3)` (Date 1 7 1990) (Date 20 6 1990))
#ASSERT NOT (`whether the amendment binds the Crown is decided by section 22(3)` (Date 20 6 1990) (Date 1 1 1980))
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act binds the Crown` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act binds the Crown` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act binds the Crown` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act binds the Crown` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act does not bind the Crown` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act does not bind the Crown` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act does not bind the Crown` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Crown's immunity extends to an agent where the Act does not bind the Crown` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to the Crown extends to the Crown in this capacity` `the Crown in right of this State` FALSE
#ASSERT `a reference to the Crown extends to the Crown in this capacity` `the Crown in any other capacity` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the Crown extends to the Crown in this capacity` `the Crown in any other capacity` FALSE)
#ASSERT `a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` `an instrumentality of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` `an officer of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` `an employee of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` `a contractor or other person who carries out functions on behalf of the Crown` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to an agent of the Crown extends to` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an agent acts within the scope of the agent's obligations` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an agent acts within the scope of the agent's obligations` FALSE)
-- s 23 to 26
#ASSERT `the day the State is taken to have been established` EQUALS Date 28 12 1836
#ASSERT `a provision has the effect it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a provision has the effect it would have had if the Australia Acts had been in operation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an Act is taken to be a public Act` (Date 2 1 1873) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `an Act is taken to be a public Act` (Date 1 1 1873) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a provision or portion of an Act needs separate enacting words to have effect as a substantive enactment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
